    <?php else: ?><p class="hint">Choose this month or a future month to build a new recommendation. Past budgets stay as they were.</p><?php endif; ?>
    <?php if ($budgetRecommendation): $proposal = $budgetRecommendation['proposal']; $advice = $budgetRecommendation['advice']; ?>
    <div class="recommendation-result">
        <?php if (($proposal['vacation_contribution_cents'] ?? 0) !== ($vacationFund['planned_contribution_cents'] ?? 0) || (($proposal['travel_fund']['kind'] ?? '') !== ($vacationFund['kind'] ?? '') && $vacationFund)): ?><p class="notice">Your Vacation Fund changed since this recommendation. Build a fresh recommendation to include the current contribution; the figures below describe the earlier plan.</p><?php endif; ?>
        <?php if (!empty($proposal['vacation_contribution_cents'])): ?><p class="hint">Vacation Fund contribution: <?= money($proposal['vacation_contribution_cents']) ?>. This is separate from the expense targets below. Cash left for expenses: <?= money($proposal['capacity_cents']) ?>.</p><?php endif; ?>
        <?php if ($budgetRecommendation['applied_at']): ?><p class="notice">This recommendation was applied. The current targets above are your active budget.</p>
        <?php elseif ($budgetRecommendation['stale']): ?><p class="notice">Your spending, cash inputs or budget changed. Build a fresh recommendation before switching.</p><?php endif; ?>
        <div class="recommendation-metrics"><div><span>Cash available</span><strong><?= money($proposal['cash_cents']) ?></strong></div><div><span>Kept aside</span><strong><?= money($proposal['reserve_cents']) ?></strong></div><div><span>Spending limit</span><strong><?= money($proposal['capacity_cents']) ?></strong></div><div><span>Recommended targets</span><strong><?= money($proposal['recommended_total_cents']) ?></strong></div></div>
        <?php if ($proposal['status'] === 'needs_history'): ?><p class="notice">We need past spending or a starting budget before making a useful recommendation. Import some history or set your current targets above.</p>
        <?php elseif ($proposal['status'] === 'shortfall'): ?><p class="notice"><strong>The protected amounts need <?= money($proposal['shortfall_cents']) ?> more than you have available.</strong> This plan does not fit yet. Check your cash inputs and minimums, review flexible commitments, or consider whether more income is needed. We haven’t lowered protected costs to pretend the numbers work.</p>
        <?php elseif ($proposal['historical_gap_cents'] > 0): ?><p><strong>Your usual pattern needs about <?= money($proposal['historical_gap_cents']) ?> more than the spending limit.</strong> The recommended amounts below require cuts. Categories marked “Cut first” take the first reductions.</p>
        <?php else: ?><p>Your planning baseline fits within your available cash. Extra room stays available rather than increasing every category.</p><?php endif; ?>
        <?php if ($proposal['unallocated_cents'] > 0 && $proposal['status'] !== 'needs_history'): ?><p class="hint"><?= money($proposal['unallocated_cents']) ?> remains unallocated, in addition to the <?= money($proposal['reserve_cents']) ?> kept aside.</p><?php endif; ?>
        <div class="table-scroll"><table class="recommendation-table"><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th class="number">Planning baseline</th><th class="number">Current budget</th><th class="number">Recommended</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <?php foreach ($proposal['groups'] as $key => $group): ?><tr><th scope="row"><?= escape($group['name']) ?><small><?= escape(budget_recommendation_reason($group)) ?><?php if ($group['cut_percent'] >= 50): ?> This is a substantial change from past spending.<?php endif; ?><?php if ($group['smoothed']): ?> A large past month was smoothed; check upcoming costs.<?php endif; ?></small></th><td class="number"><?= money($group['baseline_cents']) ?></td><td class="number"><?= !isset($budget['targets'][$key]) ? 'Not set' : money($budget['targets'][$key]) ?></td><td class="number"><strong><?= money($group['recommended_cents']) ?></strong></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?>
        </tbody><tfoot><tr><th>Total</th><td class="number"><?= money($proposal['baseline_cents']) ?></td><td class="number"><?= $budget['targets'] ? money(array_sum($budget['targets'])) : 'Not set' ?></td><td class="number"><?= money($proposal['recommended_total_cents']) ?></td></tr></tfoot></table></div>
        <?php if (!$budgetRecommendation['applied_at'] && !$budgetRecommendation['stale'] && $proposal['status'] === 'ready' && $budgetMonth >= recommendation_current_month()): ?>
        <form method="post" action="/?page=budget" class="recommendation-apply"><?php csrf_field(); ?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="apply_recommended_budget"><input type="hidden" name="budget_month" value="<?= escape($budgetMonth) ?>"><input type="hidden" name="recommendation_version" value="<?= escape($proposal['fingerprint']) ?>"><button type="submit">Apply recommended budget</button><span class="hint">Replaces <?= escape(month_label($budgetMonth)) ?> targets and carries forward until your next saved change.</span></form>
        <?php endif; ?>
        <?php if ($advice): ?><div class="recommendation-take"><h3>KLE Coin’s Take</h3><details class="review-disclosure"><summary><span class="review-teaser-text"><?= escape(month_review_teaser($advice['summary'])) ?></span> <span class="review-toggle"><svg class="review-target" viewBox="0 0 28 28" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="10" fill="#ffe58a" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="2" fill="currentColor"/><path d="M25 3 12 16m0-5v5h5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span class="review-read-more">Read now</span><span class="review-read-less">Read less</span><span class="sr-only"> about your recommended budget</span></span></summary><?php if (month_review_teaser($advice['summary']) !== $advice['summary']): ?><p><?= escape($advice['summary']) ?></p><?php endif; ?><ul><?php foreach ($advice['next_steps'] as $step): ?><li><?= escape($step) ?></li><?php endforeach; ?></ul><details><summary>Why each category changed</summary><?php foreach ($proposal['groups'] as $key => $group): ?><p><strong><?= escape($group['name']) ?>.</strong> <?= escape($advice['categories'][$key]) ?></p><?php endforeach; ?></details><p class="hint">AI-assisted explanation of this saved recommendation.</p></details></div>
        <?php elseif ($budgetRecommendation['ai_status'] === 'failed'): ?><p class="hint">The personalized explanation is unavailable. The calculated plan and category reasons above are ready to review.</p>
        <?php elseif (in_array($budgetRecommendation['ai_status'], ['pending', 'processing'], true) && category_ai_config()['enabled']): ?><p class="hint">Your personalized take is being prepared. The numbers are ready to review. <a href="/?page=budget&amp;month=<?= escape($budgetMonth) ?>#recommended-budget">Refresh</a></p><?php endif; ?>
        <p class="hint"><?php if (count($proposal['months']) < 3): ?>Limited history: <?php endif; ?><?= count($proposal['months']) ?> earlier month<?= count($proposal['months']) === 1 ? '' : 's' ?> used<?= $proposal['months'] ? ', ' . escape(month_label($proposal['months'][0])) . '–' . escape(month_label($proposal['months'][array_key_last($proposal['months'])])) : '' ?>. <?= $proposal['confirmed_count'] ?> confirmed complete.<?php if ($proposal['confirmed_count'] < count($proposal['months'])): ?> Unconfirmed history may be partial.<?php endif; ?></p>
    </div>
    <?php endif; ?>
    <details class="data-note"><summary>How we build the recommendation</summary><p>Everyday categories blend the last six available months: 70% of a recent-weighted average and 30% of the median. With at least four months, unusually large months are capped for this calculation. Travel and home improvement use up to twelve months of average spending so occasional costs still have an allowance. Travel targets cover ordinary purchases. Set a separate Vacation Fund contribution above to save for future vacations. Its planned contribution is reserved before allocating expense targets, and accumulated savings are not treated as new monthly cash. Missing months are excluded, and confirmed zero-activity months count. Purchases are used before refunds; card payments are excluded.</p><p>We reduce “Cut first” categories proportionally, then “Flexible”, then any room above a protected minimum. We never go below a minimum or spending already recorded for the selected month. This is a suggested monthly plan, not a prediction. Review the assumptions and minimums before switching.</p></details>
</section>
